        'In the photoelectric effect, light ejects electrons from a metal surface. Classical wave theory predicted that brighter light of any color would eventually free electrons, and that their energy would grow with brightness. Experiments showed neither: there is a sharp threshold frequency, emission is instant, and the electrons’ maximum energy depends only on frequency.',
