        'KE_max is measured with a stopping potential: the reverse voltage that just stops the fastest electrons, eV_stop = KE_max. A graph of KE_max against f is a straight line with slope h and intercept −φ, which Millikan used to measure Planck’s constant. Solar cells, digital cameras, and light meters rely on the photoelectric effect.',
